  "body": "Stacked on #2138. The diff against `main` also shows the commit of #2138 (e7050be17) until #2138 merges. After that merge, only the commit 3fe7da701 is in the diff.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The op stamp salt moves from `camcraft-op-stamp-v2` to `camcraft-op-stamp-v3` (`crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs`).\n- #2138 changed the rapid law. The post gate reads only the verdicts that a cache carries, and it does not run the rapid law again. A project saved before #2138 had a cache with a matching stamp. That cache posted a traverse through uncut stock with no warning.\n- Now each cache from before this change reads Stale. The post refuses it with the message `<op>: inputs moved since generation - regenerate before posting`. A regenerate judges the path under the new law.\n- The salt comment now says: bump the salt when a verify law that a cache records changes.\n- `examples/first-router-part.camproj`: the three stamps are the v3 stamps. I regenerated each operation under the new law: the same move count and no warnings. Thus the new stamps are true, and `first_router_part` still posts the committed demo.\n- `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs`: `ONE_PROFILE_STAMP` is pinned again for the new salt. The salt is the only change to that digest.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2152-stale-rapid-verdict.md`. The salt is the smaller mechanism. A project-version migration (v62 -> v63) was dropped: it gives the same result for the user, but older builds then cannot open new files. A re-run of the rapid law at post time was dropped: it is too large for a fix that holds the cut.\n\nThe project-file version does not change. Older builds open the files of this build. This is not a breaking change.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the salt change, the pin `a_cache_judged_under_the_old_rapid_law_reads_stale_and_holds_the_post` failed: the old-law cache read `Ok` (thus it posted with no warning). After the salt change, the pin passes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/stale_rapid_law.rs`:\n  - `a_cache_judged_under_the_old_rapid_law_reads_stale_and_holds_the_post`\n  - `regenerating_the_old_cache_judges_it_under_the_new_law`\n- Fixture: `crates/app/tests/stale_rapid_law/rapid_law_v2_cache.camproj`. It is the #2121 repro (a Contour with clearance and retract at Z 8, stock top Z 10), saved at e7050be17 with salt v2. I removed the two `rapid_in_stock` verdicts and the \"Clearance in stock\" note from the cache. The result is the cache that the old law wrote.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base pr-2138`: 31 app suites and the app lib. The first run failed only in `wire_stamp` (the pinned stamp value). After the re-pin, `wire_stamp` and `stale_rapid_law` pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_router_part --test clearance_in_stock`: 4 + 8 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI suites. No UI test posts a recorded project. `docs_example_steps_through_operations` checks only that each operation has a toolpath. The #371 fixture test accepts a Stale operation.\n- `examples/first-part.camproj`, the microARC kit project and the #371 UI fixture keep their old stamps. They read Stale, and they regenerate one time, as a user's project does.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Fixed: a toolpath generated before the clearance-plane rapid check (#2121) now reads stale, and the post refuses it until you regenerate it. Each saved operation regenerates one time after the upgrade.\n\nFixes #2152\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
